# LongCat-2.5-Preview — findings by Space Bunny Alpha (SELF-EXCLUDED: no verified public benchmarks)

> **Why this file is `.excluded`:** as of 2026-09-27 I found **zero verified public
> benchmark numbers** for `LongCat-2.5-Preview`. Meituan's own launch materials and
> changelog contain no 2.5-specific benchmark table, and no independent evaluator
> (Artificial Analysis, BenchLM, LLM Stats, SWE-bench, long-cat.org) has published a
> row for it. Per the template's SELF-EXCLUSION rule and `RULES.md`, this file carries
> notes only — **no scores are asserted and nothing below is counted toward any
> average.** The model shipped two days before this review, which is the likely reason.

- Source: Meituan (`LongCat-2.5-Preview`)
- Date: 2026-09-27 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card (facts only — verified, no scores)

- **Name:** LongCat-2.5-Preview
- **Short description:** Meituan's (LongCat) multimodal preview model for long-horizon
  agent work, released 2026-09-25 as the successor to LongCat-2.0. It keeps 2.0's
  advertised scale and context and adds **image understanding**; it is a *preview*
  build, so expect model-ID or behavior changes. Distinct model from LongCat-2.0 — do
  not read 2.0's scores onto it.
- **Provider / access:** LongCat API platform (`https://longcat.ai/platform/`), model ID
  `LongCat-2.5-Preview`. Both an **OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions** endpoint and an
  **Anthropic-compatible Messages** endpoint are documented; a `thinking` toggle is
  exposed on the chat endpoint. Documented integrations include Claude Code, Codex,
  OpenCode, Cline, Kilo Code, OpenClaw, CatPaw, Cherry Studio, Chatbox and Hermes Agent.
- **Release / knowledge:** released 2026-09-25 (LongCat API platform changelog,
  version 2026-09-25). Knowledge cutoff not documented.
- **IDs:** `LongCat-2.5-Preview` (Meituan first-party); canonical third-party ID
  `meituan/longcat-2.5-preview` (models.dev). On OpenCode Zen and OpenCode Go it is
  served as **`meituan/longcat-2.5-preview-free`** at **$0.00 / $0.00** (models.dev,
  both providers) — i.e. a free Zen/Go ID does exist, unlike several paid-only models in
  this dataset.
- **Context window:** **1,000,000 tokens** context, **128K (131,072) max output**
  (LongCat API quick start; models.dev lists the same 1,000,000 / 131,072 pair).
- **Modalities:** text + **image in**, text out; `thinking` reasoning toggle yes; native
  tool calling yes; temperature control exposed. **Caveat worth recording:** the
  published chat-completions reference still describes `content` as a plain-text string
  and shows no image payload, so the image path is documented in the changelog but not
  yet in the API reference (documentation gap, not evidence the capability is absent).
  No audio or video input; no non-text output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-27):** Meituan first-party, per 1M tokens —
  standard $0.75 uncached input / $0.015 cached / $2.95 output;
  **limited-time promotional $0.30 / $0.006 / $1.20**. The promo rate is identical to
  MiniMax M3's list price, not uniquely cheap. Plus **$0.00/$0.00** on OpenCode Zen/Go
  via the `-free` ID. Meituan also granted **5M free tokens to existing users** at
  launch. Free tiers carry the usual training-data-consent and time-limited caveats.
- **Architecture:** proprietary for 2.5 — **1.6T total / ~48B active** MoE (the same
  scale figures Meituan published for LongCat-2.0, so the 2.5 launch is *not* a
  parameter-count or context-length jump). No 2.5 weights published on Hugging Face;
  LongCat-2.0 was open-weighted, and that status must not be assumed for 2.5.

